# MASTER DEVELOPMENT SPECIFICATION

## Family Android Network Access Management System

You are the primary senior software architect and implementation agent for this project.

Your job is to DESIGN, IMPLEMENT, TEST, DEBUG, DOCUMENT, and ITERATE a complete production-quality system consisting of:

1. An Android client application.
2. A cloud backend/API.
3. A PostgreSQL database.
4. A web-based administrator dashboard.
5. Push communication between the backend and Android devices.
6. Optional Android Device Owner / Android Enterprise management mode.
7. Local Android traffic/session enforcement.
8. Secure Wi-Fi credential provisioning.

The system is intended for a FAMILY environment. The administrator owns/controls the network and the participating Android devices. All required permissions will be granted by the device owner.

Do not take shortcuts by building a fake UI or mock-only implementation. The final project must have real working architecture, real API communication, persistent database storage, authentication, Android networking, quota accounting, session management, and enforcement.

---

# 1. CORE PURPOSE

Build a system where family members can use an Airtel Xstream Wi-Fi connection through an Android application without being given the Wi-Fi password directly.

The Airtel router itself is NOT being modified.

The router is simply the Internet/Wi-Fi source.

The Android application controls access on each participating Android device.

The system must support:

* Admin-created user accounts.
* No public user registration.
* Secure user authentication.
* Device registration.
* Secure Wi-Fi credential delivery.
* Automatic Wi-Fi connection where Android permits it.
* Data quotas.
* Time quotas.
* Unlimited data.
* Unlimited time.
* Combined data + time limits.
* Session tracking.
* Device usage tracking.
* Background enforcement.
* Remote disable.
* Remote quota changes.
* Remote session termination.
* Usage history.
* Live device status.
* Push commands.
* Optional Device Owner management.
* Stronger VPN enforcement in managed mode.
* Recovery after reboot.
* Recovery after network loss.
* Recovery after app process restart.
* Server-authoritative quotas.

The system must NEVER claim to control the Airtel router itself.

