# 6. FIREBASE

Use Firebase Cloud Messaging for Android device commands and notifications.

Each Android installation must register its current FCM registration token with the backend.

Do not assume an FCM token is permanent.

When the token changes, update the backend.

The server must be able to send commands such as:

* CONFIG_UPDATED
* QUOTA_UPDATED
* SESSION_REVOKED
* DEVICE_DISABLED
* CREDENTIAL_VERSION_CHANGED
* FORCE_RECONNECT
* SYNC_REQUIRED

Do not put sensitive Wi-Fi passwords or other secrets directly into FCM payloads.

FCM should act as a wake-up/control signal.

The Android app should then authenticate to the backend and retrieve the authoritative configuration securely.

