# 50. SECURITY MODEL

Assume the Android client can be modified by a technically skilled user in STANDARD mode.

Therefore:

* never trust the client as the authority.
* never send unlimited privileges to the client.
* never rely solely on client-side quota calculations.
* server must validate authorization.
* client enforcement is an enforcement layer, not the ultimate authority.

MANAGED Device Owner mode provides stronger local enforcement.

